# Ruling OD-2, widened by Locked 22: a SCHEDULED job holds the one-active-job slot, enforced by the database. The fault drops 'scheduled' from the partial unique index predicate of platform_0011 (the index that platform_0004's was replaced by; a patch of platform_0004 would be dropped and re-created by 0011 and prove nothing); a second job moved previewed -> confirmed beside a scheduled one is then ALLOWED and the test must say so.
GATE=slot-scheduled
TARGET=platform
SETUP=
STEP=go test TestConstraints_Jobs (database integration test, real Postgres)
CMD=H_PG_ADMIN_DSN="$FAULT_ADMIN_DSN" bash tests/harness/run-db-tests.sh '^TestConstraints_Jobs$'
MESSAGE=--- FAIL: TestConstraints_Jobs
MESSAGE=the second job moved previewed -> confirmed while the first is scheduled: was ALLOWED
